<title>GERMANY: POLL - Economists see rise in German Feb jobless.</title>
<headline>POLL - Economists see rise in German Feb jobless.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters on Monday and Tuesday gave the following forecasts for February German jobless data which will be released on Thursday.</p>
<p>All forecasts give the absolute change expected in the seasonally adjusted figure in February compared with January. In January, there were 4.317 million unemployed on seasonally-adjusted basis, a rise of 160,000 from December.</p>
<p>						     Forecast</p>
<p> Werner Verbockett, Commerzbank	    +60,000</p>
<p> Klaus Baader, DMG, London		   +/- 0</p>
<p> Mathias Haffner, BZW			  +30,000</p>
<p> Klaus Friedrich, Dresdner Bank	    +23,000</p>
<p> Ulrike Kastens, TCM			   +20,000</p>
<p> Thomas Kull, WestLB			   +20,000</p>
<p> Armin Kayser, SBC Warburg		   +20,000</p>
<p> Ralf Kugelstadt, UBS			  -5,000</p>
<p> Gerhard Lyons, DKB International	  +35,000</p>
<p> Hugh Roberts, Nat West Markets	    +35,000</p>
<p> Dr. Gerhard Grebe, Bank Julius Baer     -40,000</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
